  "body": "## What is wrong\n\n`plan_level` adds the `AIR_ENTRY` note and does not look at the tool.\nFor a tool that is not centre-cutting, the ladder keeps the old entry law.\nThen the note and the posted program do not agree. The message is misleading.\n\n## Where\n\n- `crates/motion/src/machining3d/hsm.rs:234-237`\n- `crates/motion/src/machining3d/ladder.rs:195`\n\n## Source\n\nThe read-only Opus review of the merged PR #2035 found this defect:\nhttps://github.com/NeoTech/Camcraft/pull/2035#issuecomment-6972199583\n\nThe review read the diff only. It did not build and it ran no test.\nThe posted toolpath is not changed by this defect. Only the note is wrong.\n\n## Done when\n\n- The note appears only when the level uses the air entry.\n- A test pins the two cases: a centre-cutting tool and a tool that is not centre-cutting.\n",
